## 🐛 Race Condition: Form Submit Listener

**Issue:** Event listener is attached but never cleaned up, causing memory leaks when the controller is destroyed and recreated (e.g., during Turbo navigation).

**Problem:**
- Multiple instances will create multiple listeners
- No cleanup in `disconnect()` lifecycle hook

**Fix Required:**
```javascript
connect() {
  this.fieldCount = 0
  this.fields = []
  this.loadExistingData()

  // Bind handler to maintain context
  this.boundSubmitHandler = this.handleSubmit.bind(this)
  const form = this.element.closest('form')
  if (form) {
    form.addEventListener('submit', this.boundSubmitHandler, { capture: true })
  }
}

disconnect() {
  // Clean up event listener to prevent memory leaks
  const form = this.element.closest('form')
  if (form && this.boundSubmitHandler) {
    form.removeEventListener('submit', this.boundSubmitHandler, { capture: true })
  }
}

handleSubmit(event) {
  this.updateJsonField()
}
```

**Priority:** HIGH - This will cause memory leaks in production

## 🐛 JavaScript Issue: `dynamic_fields_controller.js`

### Issue 1: Memory Leak - Event Listener Not Cleaned Up

**File:** `app/javascript/controllers/dynamic_fields_controller.js`

**Current Code (Lines 6-15):**
```javascript
connect() {
  this.fieldCount = 0
  this.fields = []
  this.loadExistingData()

  // Update JSON before form submission (capture phase to run before Turbo)
  const form = this.element.closest('form')
  if (form) {
    form.addEventListener('submit', () => this.updateJsonField(), { capture: true })
  }
}
```

**Problems:**
1. ❌ No `disconnect()` method to remove event listener
2. ❌ Arrow function creates new reference each time - can't be removed
3. ❌ Multiple controller instances = multiple listeners on same form
4. ❌ Turbo navigation will destroy/recreate controllers = memory leak

**Fix Required:**
```javascript
connect() {
  this.fieldCount = 0
  this.fields = []
  this.loadExistingData()

  // Bind handler to maintain context for cleanup
  this.boundSubmitHandler = this.handleSubmit.bind(this)
  const form = this.element.closest('form')
  if (form) {
    form.addEventListener('submit', this.boundSubmitHandler, { capture: true })
  }
}

disconnect() {
  // Critical: Clean up event listener to prevent memory leaks
  const form = this.element.closest('form')
  if (form && this.boundSubmitHandler) {
    form.removeEventListener('submit', this.boundSubmitHandler, { capture: true })
  }
}

handleSubmit(event) {
  this.updateJsonField()
}
```

---

### Issue 2: Missing Error Handling for JSON Parsing

**File:** `app/javascript/controllers/dynamic_fields_controller.js`

**Current Code (Lines 18-30):**
```javascript
loadExistingData() {
  const hiddenField = document.querySelector('[name="product[specification_pdp]"]')

  if (hiddenField && hiddenField.value) {
    try {
      const data = JSON.parse(hiddenField.value)
      // ... populate fields
    } catch (e) {
      console.error('Error parsing specification_pdp JSON:', e)
      this.addField()  // Just adds empty field, user doesn't know what happened
    }
  }
}
```

**Problems:**
1. ❌ Silent failure - user has no idea JSON parsing failed
2. ❌ Corrupted data will just show empty form
3. ❌ No way for user to recover or fix the issue

**Fix Required:**
```javascript
loadExistingData() {
  const hiddenField = document.querySelector('[name="product[specification_pdp]"]')

  if (hiddenField && hiddenField.value) {
    try {
      const rawValue = hiddenField.value.trim()
      if (rawValue && rawValue !== '{}' && rawValue !== '[]') {
        const data = JSON.parse(rawValue)

        // Validate structure
        if (typeof data !== 'object' || data === null) {
          throw new Error('Invalid specification format')
        }

        // Populate fields from existing data
        Object.keys(data).forEach(groupName => {
          const groupFields = data[groupName]
          if (Array.isArray(groupFields)) {
            groupFields.forEach(field => {
              this.addFieldWithData(groupName, field.name, field.value)
            })
          }
        })
      } else {
        this.addField()
      }
    } catch (e) {
      console.error('Failed to parse specification_pdp:', e)

      // Show user-friendly error message
      this.showError(
        'Failed to load existing specifications. The data may be corrupted. ' +
        'Please refresh the page or contact support if the issue persists.'
      )

      // Add one empty field so form is still usable
      this.addField()
    }
  } else {
    this.addField()
  }
}

showError(message) {
  // Create error notification
  const errorDiv = document.createElement('div')
  errorDiv.className = 'bg-red-100 border border-red-400 text-red-700 px-4 py-3 rounded mb-4'
  errorDiv.innerHTML = `
    <strong class="font-bold">Error!</strong>
    <span class="block sm:inline">${message}</span>
  `
  this.element.prepend(errorDiv)

  // Auto-remove after 10 seconds
  setTimeout(() => errorDiv.remove(), 10000)
}
```

---

### Issue 3: XSS Risk in `escapeHtml()`

**File:** `app/javascript/controllers/dynamic_fields_controller.js`

**Current Code (Lines 67-72):**
```javascript
escapeHtml(text) {
  const div = document.createElement('div')
  div.textContent = text
  return div.innerHTML
}
```

**Problem:**
This is actually GOOD for escaping, but the values are then used in template literals which can still be problematic.

**Better Approach - Use DOM APIs directly:**
```javascript
addFieldWithData(group = '', name = '', value = '') {
  const fieldHtml = `
    <div class="flex items-center space-x-2 mb-2" data-field-index="${this.fieldCount}">
      <input type="text"
             placeholder="Group"
             class="flex-1 px-3 py-2 border border-gray-300 rounded-lg"
             data-action="input->dynamic-fields#updateField"
             data-field-type="group">
      <input type="text"
             placeholder="Name"
             class="flex-1 px-3 py-2 border border-gray-300 rounded-lg"
             data-action="input->dynamic-fields#updateField"
             data-field-type="name">
      <input type="text"
             placeholder="Value"
             class="flex-1 px-3 py-2 border border-gray-300 rounded-lg"
             data-action="input->dynamic-fields#updateField"
             data-field-type="value">
      <button type="button"
              class="text-red-500 hover:text-red-700 p-2"
              data-action="click->dynamic-fields#removeField">
        <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M6 18L18 6M6 6l12 12"></path>
        </svg>
      </button>
    </div>
  `

  this.containerTarget.insertAdjacentHTML('beforeend', fieldHtml)

  // Set values using DOM APIs (browser handles escaping automatically)
  const newField = this.containerTarget.lastElementChild
  newField.querySelector('[data-field-type="group"]').value = group
  newField.querySelector('[data-field-type="name"]').value = name
  newField.querySelector('[data-field-type="value"]').value = value

  this.fieldCount++
}
```

**Priority:** HIGH - Memory leak will affect production, error handling improves UX

