## 📁 File Review: `app/javascript/controllers/product_details_controller.js`

### Current Changes (Lines 115-180)

**What Changed:**
- Added prioritization of `specification_pdp` over legacy `specification`
- Added rendering for NEW grouped format: `{"Group": [{"name": "Field", "value": "Value"}]}`
- Maintained backward compatibility with old array/object formats

### Issues Found:

#### 🐛 Issue: Inconsistent Fallback Logic

**Line 117:**
```javascript
const specification = parseSpecification(product.specification_pdp || product.specification);
```

**Problem:**
- Empty string `''` is truthy in JavaScript, so `|| fallback` won't work
- `'{}'` and `'[]'` are also truthy but represent empty data
- Will try to parse empty strings and fail silently

**Fix Required:**
```javascript
const specification = parseSpecification(
  getValidSpecification(product)
);

function getValidSpecification(product) {
  // Helper to check if spec data is valid
  const isValidSpec = (spec) => {
    if (!spec) return false;
    const trimmed = spec.trim();
    return trimmed && trimmed !== '{}' && trimmed !== '[]';
  };

  // Prioritize specification_pdp
  if (isValidSpec(product.specification_pdp)) {
    return product.specification_pdp;
  }

  // Fallback to legacy specification
  if (isValidSpec(product.specification)) {
    return product.specification;
  }

  return null;
}
```

---

#### 🐛 Issue: No Error Handling for JSON Parsing

**Lines 120-180:**
The `parseSpecification` function doesn't handle JSON parse errors.

**Risk:** Corrupted specification data will break the product details page.

**Fix Required:**
```javascript
const parseSpecification = (spec) => {
  if (!spec) return null;

  try {
    return typeof spec === 'string' ? JSON.parse(spec) : spec;
  } catch (e) {
    console.error('Failed to parse specification:', e);
    // Return null to show "No specification available" instead of breaking page
    return null;
  }
};
```

---

#### 🎯 Enhancement: Add Type Guards

**Lines 122-150:** The NEW format detection logic could be more robust.

**Current Code:**
```javascript
if (typeof spec === 'object' && spec !== null && !Array.isArray(spec)) {
  const firstKey = Object.keys(spec)[0];
  const firstValue = spec[firstKey];

  if (firstValue && Array.isArray(firstValue) && firstValue.length > 0 &&
      firstValue[0].hasOwnProperty('name') && firstValue[0].hasOwnProperty('value')) {
    // Render new format
  }
}
```

**Suggested Improvement:**
```javascript
// Add helper function for type checking
function isGroupedSpecFormat(spec) {
  if (typeof spec !== 'object' || spec === null || Array.isArray(spec)) {
    return false;
  }

  // Check if at least one group exists with valid structure
  const groups = Object.values(spec);
  return groups.length > 0 && groups.every(group => {
    return Array.isArray(group) && group.every(field => 
      field && 
      typeof field === 'object' && 
      field.hasOwnProperty('name') && 
      field.hasOwnProperty('value')
    );
  });
}

// Use in rendering logic
if (isGroupedSpecFormat(spec)) {
  return renderGroupedSpecification(spec);
}
```

---

#### 🔒 Security: XSS Prevention

**Lines 130-145:** Group names and field values are inserted directly into HTML.

**Current Code:**
```javascript
const groupHeader = `
  <tr>
    <th colspan="2" class="p-2 border-b bg-gray-100 font-semibold text-gray-700 text-left">${groupName}</th>
  </tr>`;

const groupRows = fields.map(field => `
  <tr>
    <td class="p-2 border-b pl-4">${field.name}</td>
    <td class="p-2 border-b">${field.value}</td>
  </tr>`).join('');
```

**Risk:** If specification data contains malicious HTML/JS, it will be executed.

**Fix Required:**
```javascript
// Add HTML escaping helper
function escapeHtml(text) {
  const div = document.createElement('div');
  div.textContent = text;
  return div.innerHTML;
}

// Use in rendering
const groupHeader = `
  <tr>
    <th colspan="2" class="p-2 border-b bg-gray-100 font-semibold text-gray-700 text-left">${escapeHtml(groupName)}</th>
